        "original_id": "465c16c0-2d78-56e5-bef8-f2da73736473",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Angelique Kerber, Amélie Mauresmo, Victoria Azarenka\n- Roles: world No. 1 tennis players\n- Events: 2004 Summer Olympics, Australian Open, Wimbledon\n\nFacts:\n- Amélie Mauresmo was born on 5 July 1979 and is a French former professional tennis player and former world No. 1.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won a silver medal at the 2004 Summer Olympics.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won two Grand Slam singles titles at the Australian Open and Wimbledon.\n- Angelique Kerber became world No. 1 on 12 September 2016.\n- Angelique Kerber was the twenty-second player and the oldest player to reach world No. 1 for the first time.\n- Angelique Kerber was the first new world No. 1 since Victoria Azarenka in 2012.",
